###Text
Text test::oliveharbor::doc::ScopeNote
{
  type: markdown;
  content: '# Ferry Sailing Notice Scope\n\nThis model describes the intended scope of the ferry sailing-notice\nnormalisation surface for a coastal passenger terminal.\n\n* A sailing notice arrives as a single delimited text payload composed of\n  labelled sections: the terminal identifier, an optional advisory note and a\n  list-valued berth allocation.\n* The published surface is one document-returning endpoint. It carries no\n  store binding: the payload itself is the source, and the normalised JSON\n  document is the response.\n* Section labels are case-insensitive on input and normalised to upper case on\n  output, so a notice re-issued with different casing produces an identical\n  document.\n* Berth entries that carry no code are dropped rather than published as empty\n  members, and an absent advisory section is published as an explicit null.\n\nNothing in this element is executed; it exists so that the compiled element\nset carries the scope statement alongside the endpoint it describes.';
}
